================================================================================
  VESC FIRMWARE FLASHING GUIDE — FOR BEGINNERS / PANDUAN UNTUK PEMULA
  Target Hardware : Custom BLDC Controller (STM32F405 + DRV8302)
  Firmware Source : https://github.com/vedderb/bldc
  Last Updated    : 2025
================================================================================

IMPORTANT NOTE / CATATAN PENTING
----------------------------------
ID: Panduan ini ditujukan untuk orang yang baru pertama kali bekerja dengan
    STM32 dan VESC firmware. Berbeda dengan ESP32 yang tinggal colok USB dan
    upload lewat Arduino IDE, STM32 kosong (fresh from factory) TIDAK punya
    bootloader bawaan. Artinya kamu WAJIB melakukan flash pertama kali
    menggunakan programmer fisik (ST-Link) sebelum bisa menggunakan VESC Tool.

EN: This guide is intended for those who are new to STM32 and VESC firmware.
    Unlike ESP32 which just needs a USB cable and Arduino IDE, a blank STM32
    (fresh from factory) does NOT have a built-in bootloader. This means you
    MUST perform the first flash using a physical programmer (ST-Link) before
    you can use VESC Tool.


================================================================================
  WHAT YOU NEED / APA YANG DIBUTUHKAN
================================================================================

Hardware:
  - Custom BLDC board (STM32F405 + DRV8302)
  - ST-Link V3MINIE (recommended) — official from STMicroelectronics
    * Lebih cepat dan reliable dibanding ST-Link V2 clone
    * Faster and more reliable than ST-Link V2 clones
  - Kabel jumper / Jumper wires (minimal 4 kabel: SWDIO, SWCLK, GND, 3.3V)

Software (Windows):
  - ARM GNU Toolchain   : https://developer.arm.com/downloads
  - Make for Windows    : via Chocolatey (lihat Step 1.3)
  - Git                 : https://git-scm.com
  - STM32CubeProgrammer : https://www.st.com/en/development-tools/stm32cubeprog.html
  - VESC Tool (optional, untuk fase 2) : https://vesc-project.com

================================================================================
  FASE 1 — FIRST TIME FLASH (WAJIB ST-LINK / MANDATORY ST-LINK)
================================================================================

ID: Fase ini wajib dilakukan SATU KALI di awal, sebelum apapun bisa dilakukan
    lewat USB. Semua step di bawah dilakukan di PC kamu.

EN: This phase is mandatory and done ONCE at the beginning, before anything
    can be done via USB. All steps below are performed on your PC.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 1 — INSTALL TOOLCHAIN (Setup Kompiler / Setup Compiler)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  STEP 1.1 — ARM GNU Toolchain (Compiler)
  -----------------------------------------
  ID: Ini adalah compiler-nya — software yang mengubah kode C/C++ menjadi
      machine code yang dimengerti oleh processor ARM Cortex-M4 di STM32F405.
      Tanpa ini, source code VESC tidak bisa diubah menjadi file binary (.bin).

  EN: This is the compiler — software that converts C/C++ source code into
      machine code understood by the ARM Cortex-M4 processor in STM32F405.
      Without this, VESC source code cannot be converted into a binary file.

  - Download: https://developer.arm.com/downloads/-/arm-gnu-toolchain-downloads
  - Pilih versi: arm-gnu-toolchain-...-mingw-w64-x86_64-arm-none-eabi.exe
  - Install, lalu tambahkan path install ke Environment Variable PATH Windows.
    Contoh path: C:\Program Files (x86)\Arm GNU Toolchain arm-none-eabi\13.x\bin
  - Verifikasi di Command Prompt:
      arm-none-eabi-gcc --version

  STEP 1.2 — Git
  ---------------
  ID: Digunakan untuk mengunduh (clone) source code VESC firmware dari GitHub.

  EN: Used to download (clone) the VESC firmware source code from GitHub.

  - Download: https://git-scm.com/download/win
  - Install dengan pengaturan default.
  - Verifikasi: git --version

  STEP 1.3 — Make (via Chocolatey)
  ----------------------------------
  ID: Make adalah tool yang membaca file Makefile di dalam folder VESC dan
      mengatur urutan kompilasi ratusan file C secara otomatis. Tanpa Make,
      kamu harus mengetik command compiler satu per satu — tidak praktis.

  EN: Make is a tool that reads the Makefile inside the VESC folder and
      automatically manages the compilation order of hundreds of C files.
      Without Make, you would need to type compiler commands one by one.

  - Buka PowerShell sebagai Administrator / Open PowerShell as Administrator
  - Install Chocolatey (package manager untuk Windows):

      Set-ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Scope Process -Force; `
      iwr https://chocolatey.org/install.ps1 -UseBasicParsing | iex

  - Install Make:
      choco install make

  - Verifikasi: make --version

  STEP 1.4 — STM32CubeProgrammer
  --------------------------------
  ID: Software resmi dari ST untuk mem-flash file binary ke STM32 melalui
      ST-Link. Ini pengganti "upload" button di Arduino IDE.

  EN: Official software from ST to flash binary files to STM32 via ST-Link.
      This is the equivalent of the "upload" button in Arduino IDE.

  - Download: https://www.st.com/en/development-tools/stm32cubeprog.html
    (perlu registrasi akun ST / requires ST account registration)
  - Install dengan pengaturan default, termasuk driver ST-Link.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 2 — CLONE VESC FIRMWARE (Download Source Code)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  ID: Source code VESC firmware diunduh dari GitHub menggunakan Git. Ini bukan
      file siap pakai — ini adalah kode sumber yang harus dikompilasi terlebih
      dahulu menjadi file .bin sesuai hardware kamu.

  EN: VESC firmware source code is downloaded from GitHub using Git. This is
      NOT a ready-to-use file — it is source code that must be compiled first
      into a .bin file matching your hardware.

  - Buka Command Prompt / Git Bash, navigasi ke folder pilihan kamu, lalu:

      git clone https://github.com/vedderb/bldc.git
      cd bldc

  - Struktur folder penting:
      bldc/
      ├── main.c          → Entry point firmware
      ├── Makefile        → Instruksi build / Build instructions
      ├── hwconf/         → Konfigurasi hardware per board (pin mapping, dll)
      ├── mc_interface.c  → Logika motor control / Motor control logic
      └── ChibiOS/        → RTOS yang digunakan VESC / RTOS used by VESC

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 3 — PILIH HARDWARE TARGET / SELECT HARDWARE TARGET
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  ID: VESC firmware mendukung banyak varian board (VESC 4, VESC 6, dll).
      Kamu harus memberitahu compiler board mana yang sedang dikompilasi,
      karena setiap board punya pin mapping yang berbeda.
      Untuk board berbasis VESC 4.12, target yang digunakan adalah hw_410_412.

  EN: VESC firmware supports many board variants (VESC 4, VESC 6, etc.).
      You need to tell the compiler which board is being compiled, because
      each board has different pin mappings.
      For VESC 4.12-based boards, the target used is hw_410_412.

  - Buka file Makefile di folder bldc, cari baris:
      HWVER = 410_412

  - Jika kamu memodifikasi pin dari referensi VESC 4.12, edit file:
      hwconf/hw_410_412.h
    Sesuaikan definisi pin dengan hardware kamu.

  CATATAN / NOTE:
  ID: Jika pin mapping board kamu identik dengan VESC 4.12 original,
      tidak perlu mengubah apapun di step ini untuk uji awal.
  EN: If your board's pin mapping is identical to the original VESC 4.12,
      no changes are needed here for initial testing.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 4 — COMPILE FIRMWARE (Mengubah Source Code menjadi File Binary)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  ID: Ini adalah proses mengubah source code (.c/.h) menjadi file binary
      (.bin) yang bisa di-flash ke STM32. Proses ini dilakukan sepenuhnya
      di PC kamu menggunakan ARM GNU Toolchain + Make yang sudah diinstall.
      TIDAK memerlukan koneksi ke board sama sekali.

  EN: This is the process of converting source code (.c/.h) into a binary
      file (.bin) that can be flashed to the STM32. This process runs entirely
      on your PC using the installed ARM GNU Toolchain + Make.
      Does NOT require any connection to the board.

  COMPILE LEWAT / COMPILE VIA: Command Prompt / Terminal
  --------------------------------------------------------
  - Pastikan kamu berada di folder bldc:
      cd path/ke/folder/bldc

  - Jalankan kompilasi:
      make -j4

    ID: Flag -j4 artinya gunakan 4 proses paralel untuk mempercepat kompilasi.
        Sesuaikan angkanya dengan jumlah core CPU kamu (misal -j8 untuk 8 core).
    EN: The -j4 flag means use 4 parallel processes to speed up compilation.
        Adjust the number to your CPU core count (e.g. -j8 for 8 cores).

  - Output yang dihasilkan (di folder build/):
      BLDC_4_ChibiOS.elf   → Binary dengan debug info (untuk debugging)
      BLDC_4_ChibiOS.bin   → Binary murni (INI yang di-flash ke STM32)

  TROUBLESHOOTING COMPILE:
  ID: Jika muncul error saat compile, kemungkinan besar penyebabnya adalah:
      - Path ARM GNU Toolchain belum masuk ke Environment Variable PATH
      - Make belum terinstall dengan benar
      - Dependency/submodule belum di-init (jalankan: git submodule update --init)
  EN: If errors occur during compile, the most likely causes are:
      - ARM GNU Toolchain path not added to Environment Variable PATH
      - Make not installed correctly
      - Dependencies/submodules not initialized (run: git submodule update --init)

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 5 — SAMBUNGKAN ST-LINK KE BOARD / CONNECT ST-LINK TO BOARD
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  ID: ST-Link dihubungkan ke konektor SWD di board (P2 pada skematik).
      SWD (Serial Wire Debug) adalah protokol 2-wire untuk programming dan
      debugging STM32 — lebih simpel dari JTAG yang butuh 4-5 kabel.

  EN: ST-Link connects to the SWD connector on the board (P2 in the schematic).
      SWD (Serial Wire Debug) is a 2-wire protocol for programming and debugging
      STM32 — simpler than JTAG which requires 4-5 wires.

  Koneksi / Connection:
  ┌─────────────────────┬──────────────────────┐
  │ ST-Link V3MINIE     │ Board (P2 Schematic) │
  ├─────────────────────┼──────────────────────┤
  │ SWDIO               │ PA13 / SWDIO         │
  │ SWCLK               │ PA14 / SWCLK         │
  │ GND                 │ GND                  │
  │ 3.3V (opsional)     │ 3.3V (optional)      │
  └─────────────────────┴──────────────────────┘

  CATATAN / NOTE:
  ID: 3.3V dari ST-Link hanya cukup untuk menyalakan MCU saja (bukan power
      staging). Untuk uji pertama flash saja, ini sudah cukup.
  EN: 3.3V from ST-Link is only enough to power the MCU (not the power stage).
      For initial flash testing only, this is sufficient.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STEP 6 — FLASH FIRMWARE KE STM32 / FLASH FIRMWARE TO STM32
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  ID: File .bin yang dihasilkan dari Step 4 sekarang di-flash ke memory
      internal STM32F405 menggunakan STM32CubeProgrammer. Proses ini mirip
      dengan "upload" di Arduino IDE, tapi dilakukan via ST-Link bukan USB.

  EN: The .bin file generated in Step 4 is now flashed to the internal memory
      of STM32F405 using STM32CubeProgrammer. This is similar to "upload" in
      Arduino IDE, but done via ST-Link instead of USB.

  Langkah / Steps:
  1. Buka STM32CubeProgrammer
  2. Pilih koneksi: ST-LINK (dropdown kanan atas)
  3. Klik "Connect" — pastikan ST-Link terdeteksi dan terhubung ke board
  4. Klik "Open file" → pilih file BLDC_4_ChibiOS.bin dari folder build/
  5. Klik "Download"
  6. Tunggu hingga selesai → klik "Disconnect"
  7. Reset board (tekan tombol reset atau cabut-pasang power)

  ID: Setelah step ini selesai, STM32 kamu sudah memiliki VESC firmware
      dan siap digunakan / dikonfigurasi.
  EN: After this step, your STM32 now has VESC firmware and is ready
      to be used / configured.

================================================================================
  FASE 2 — FIRMWARE UPDATE (SETELAH FASE 1 SELESAI / AFTER PHASE 1 IS DONE)
================================================================================

  ID: Setelah Fase 1 selesai dan VESC firmware sudah ada di STM32, update
      firmware berikutnya bisa dilakukan lewat USB menggunakan VESC Tool —
      TANPA perlu ST-Link lagi.

  EN: After Phase 1 is complete and VESC firmware is on the STM32, future
      firmware updates can be done via USB using VESC Tool —
      WITHOUT needing ST-Link anymore.

  Langkah / Steps:
  1. Compile firmware baru (ulangi Step 4) → dapat .bin baru
  2. Colok USB board ke PC / Connect board USB to PC
  3. Buka VESC Tool
  4. Connect ke board (pilih port yang muncul)
  5. Pergi ke menu Firmware → Upload
  6. Pilih file .bin baru → Upload
  7. Tunggu hingga selesai → board restart otomatis

  ID: VESC Tool juga digunakan untuk konfigurasi motor (deteksi parameter,
      tuning FOC/BLDC, setting arus, dll) — bukan hanya untuk update firmware.
  EN: VESC Tool is also used for motor configuration (parameter detection,
      FOC/BLDC tuning, current settings, etc.) — not just for firmware updates.

================================================================================
  RINGKASAN ALUR / FLOW SUMMARY
================================================================================

  FASE 1 (First time):
  Source code (.c/.h)
        ↓  arm-none-eabi-gcc + make  [di PC / on PC]
  Binary (.bin)
        ↓  STM32CubeProgrammer + ST-Link  [via SWD]
  Flash memory STM32F405
        ↓
  VESC Firmware berjalan / VESC Firmware running

  FASE 2 (Update berikutnya / Subsequent updates):
  Binary (.bin) baru
        ↓  VESC Tool  [via USB]
  Flash memory STM32F405
        ↓
  Firmware updated

